Chapter: T3 Aggregates

 The v2 gate program for the T3ISA plug. Where gate.codex asks whether
 arithmetic and control flow cross a non-binary boundary, this one asks
 whether AGGREGATES do: a record on a word-addressed machine with no bytes,
 a variant with a tag, and a match that takes one apart.

 It is built to make a wrong answer visible rather than to exercise a
 feature list. The record is constructed with its fields in the OPPOSITE
 order to their declaration, so an emitter that stored by written position
 rather than by declared index reports 3 and 7 the wrong way round. The
 payloads are distinct, so a value read from the wrong offset cannot
 coincide with a right one.

 Every band is written out. `Small = Integer between 0 and 1000000` would be
 a nominally distinct type rather than an alias, so the band is repeated:
 a bare Integer is the full 64-bit range and does not fit a 27-trit word.

Section: Body

  Point = record {
   px : Integer between 0 and 1000000,
   py : Integer between 0 and 1000000
  }

  Segment = record {
   from-pt : Point,
   to-pt : Point
  }

  Tri = TFalse | TUnknown | TTrue

  Shape =
   | Dot
   | Line (Integer between 0 and 1000000)
   | Rect (Integer between 0 and 1000000) (Integer between 0 and 1000000)

 Kleene disjunction, the three-valued logic this machine's TMIN and TMAX
 implement natively. Here it is a match over three nullary constructors,
 which is the shape carrying no payload at all.

  tri-code : Tri -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  tri-code (t) = __narrow (when t
   is TFalse -> 0
   is TUnknown -> 1
   is TTrue -> 2)

  tri-or : Tri, Tri -> Tri
  tri-or (a) (b) = when a
   is TTrue -> TTrue
   is TFalse -> b
   is TUnknown -> tri-or-unknown b

  tri-or-unknown : Tri -> Tri
  tri-or-unknown (b) = when b
   is TTrue -> TTrue
   is otherwise -> TUnknown

 A match with payloads and bindings. The guarded shape is written as an if
 inside the arm, which is where a Cons-style guard would have to go anyway.

  area : Shape -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  area (s) = __narrow (when s
   is Dot -> 0
   is Line (n) -> n
   is Rect (w) (h) -> if w == h then 100 else w * h)

  manhattan : Point -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  manhattan (p) = p.px + p.py

 Built with the fields in the opposite order to their declaration. This is
 the arm that distinguishes an emitter resolving field indices from the type
 definition from one storing by written position.

  swapped : Integer between 0 and 1000000, Integer between 0 and 1000000 -> Point
  swapped (a) (b) = Point { py = b, px = a }

 A record nested in a record, so the pointer stored in a field has to be a
 pointer the reader can follow.

  seg-span : Segment -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  seg-span (s) = manhattan (s.to-pt) - manhattan (s.from-pt)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let p = swapped 3 7
    in print-line-uni ("point = " & show (p.px) & " " & show (p.py))
    let q = swapped 3 7
    in print-line-uni ("manhattan = " & show (manhattan q))
    let s = Segment { from-pt = swapped 1 1, to-pt = swapped 4 6 }
    in print-line-uni ("span = " & show (seg-span s))
    print-line-uni ("dot = " & show (area Dot))
    print-line-uni ("line 11 = " & show (area (Line 11)))
    print-line-uni ("rect 3 4 = " & show (area (Rect 3 4)))
    print-line-uni ("rect 5 5 = " & show (area (Rect 5 5)))
    print-line-uni ("or F U = " & show (tri-code (tri-or TFalse TUnknown)))
    print-line-uni ("or U T = " & show (tri-code (tri-or TUnknown TTrue)))
    print-line-uni ("or U U = " & show (tri-code (tri-or TUnknown TUnknown)))
    print-line-uni ("or F F = " & show (tri-code (tri-or TFalse TFalse)))
  end
